REDIRECT-LOOP LEG (criterion 5, Android leg) - authorize+callback MECHANISM PROVEN, full loop BLOCKED at token exchange:
- Tapping "Sign in with Mock" opens the Custom Tab at http://127.0.0.1:8755/mock/authorize (via adb reverse), the mock auto-approves and 302s to nsh.auth.sandbox://callback?code=...&state=..., Android routes it through the manifest intent filter back into MainActivity, the demo parses and validates it and attempts the token exchange. Server side confirms: mock /__control showed codes incrementing (6 codes outstanding after the runs; the 1 refreshToken/1 accessToken pair belongs to the concurrent iOS-simulator run against this same server, whose own 8755 start crashed EADDRINUSE - see docs/evidence/ios/mock-server.log).
- The token exchange then fails inside the app with: "request failed: TypeError: Network request failed: fetch POST http://127.0.0.1:8755/mock/token is not granted: add `127.0.0.1` to capabilities.network in nsh.json". Screen saved: docs/evidence/mock/android-loop-blocked.png
- ROOT CAUSE (verified in the installed APK and still present in the tree): the embedding host calls nsh.setGrantedCapabilities(HOST_GRANT) with only {"host":[...channel names...]}. Per nsh-core 0.4.0 src/access.rs (line ~1142: f(&self.declared) && self.granted.as_ref().is_none_or(f)) the grant is a CEILING, so every network fetch is denied regardless of the demo's nsh.json hosts ["127.0.0.1","localhost","10.0.2.2"]. The iOS host does it right: examples/host-ios/Sources/AppDelegate.swift grants {"host":["auth.*"],"network":{"hosts":["127.0.0.1","localhost"]}} with a comment saying exactly this. examples/host-android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/nshauth/sandbox/MainActivity.kt HOST_GRANT lacks the network entry - mock loop/storage proofs on Android stay blocked until it is added and the host rebuilt.
- Second defect in the INSTALLED APK only (stale bundle): launch extras are ignored - with --es mockBaseUrl http://10.0.2.2:9999 the app still fetched http://127.0.0.1:8755/mock/token and nothing ever connected to a listener on 9999; --es provider never auto-started a flow either. The current tree's AuthHostModule.kt normalizeMockUrl (loopback->10.0.2.2 on emulators) and host.params wiring are newer than the baked bundle; a rebuild per the final whole-tree smoke should cover this part, but NOT the missing network grant above.

