MOCK LOOP (criterion 5) - still FAIL, new deterministic blocker past the network fix:
  The flow runs authorize -> Custom Tab -> mock auto-approve -> nsh.auth.sandbox://callback
  intent-filter return -> token exchange SUCCESS (server-side) -> then the app FATALY CRASHES:
    java.lang.IllegalStateException: auth.store.save requires {"value": string}
      at dev.nshauth.sandbox.MainActivity.requireString(MainActivity.kt:102)
      at dev.nshauth.sandbox.MainActivity.installAuthHandlers$lambda$12(MainActivity.kt:71)
  Reproduced 3x (pids 4229 @09:58:10, 4339 @09:59:19, 4617 @10:01:53). Crash dialog
  screenshot: docs/evidence/mock/android-loop-crash.png ("nsh-auth sandbox keeps stopping").
  ROOT CAUSE: packages/nsh-auth/src/host.ts line 35 calls
      host.call("auth.store.save", { key: this.key, value: session })
  passing the session OBJECT, while the Android host contract (examples/host-android
  README: "{key, value} (strings)") is enforced by MainActivity.requireString, which
  throws IllegalStateException on the main thread -> process death before session.set()
  renders or persists anything. The iOS host is lenient (native/ios AuthHostModule.swift
  canonicalValue accepts "a string or a JSON object or array"), which is why the iOS loop
  passed and masked this. The load side (host.ts:20-21) already expects "the value as a
  JSON string" - save must JSON.stringify. Fix belongs in the ts package (or the Android
  host must relax like iOS); outside this task's evidence-only mandate.

  Mechanism evidence captured in system logcat (fresh buffer, 1,204 lines):
    - ActivityTaskManager START dat=http://127.0.0.1:8755/mock/authorize?response_type=code&client_id=nsh-auth-sandbox-client&redirect_uri=nsh.auth.sandbox%3A%2F%2Fcallback&scope=openid+profile+email+offline_access&state=rv6YIkBYmMxcpVnxUXvbxQ&nonce=ssXK67ITgePQaxK9voOx7A&code_challenge=-WaCPQLw7zBURWWEdRcSDJFAMD2YDQuhPSUszMXPHkw&code_challenge_method=S256 from uid 10231 (our app)
    - ActivityTaskManager START {act=VIEW cat=[BROWSABLE] dat=nsh.auth.sandbox://callback/... } from uid 10165 (Chrome) -> dev.nshauth.sandbox/.MainActivity LAUNCH_SINGLE_TASK (the intent-filter return leg)
    - FATAL EXCEPTION 30 ms later.
  Notes: (a) the emulator was found shut down (snapshot saved, not by this session) at
  ~09:50 and rebooted; the mock also died once and was restarted on 8755; adb reverse
  tcp:8755 re-applied after each. (b) --es provider/--es mockBaseUrl extras still did
  not steer the app (no autoStart; authorize used the default 127.0.0.1:8755 base, not
  the rewritten 10.0.2.2), so the demo's Mock button was pressed - the README's
  documented equivalent.

